/* GENERATED by tools/gen_data.py from docs/lore/*.json — do not edit by hand. */
const LORE = {"codex":{"republic_shattered":{"id":"republic_shattered","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE WOUNDED REPUBLIC","text":"Three wars in one lifetime have left the Republic thin as old cloth. Its senators speak of order while its fleets count their losses. Judicial patrols still walk the trade lanes, but many worlds once held by Sith lords wait for someone to remember them. Trust is scarce. Strangers are watched."},"judicial_forces":{"id":"judicial_forces","cat":"FACTION","title":"JUDICIAL FORCES","text":"The Republic's law-keepers wear grey plate over duraweave and carry carbines issued by the thousand. Their corvettes patrol the trade lanes, boarding anything that smells of contraband. Ask them about the Sith and they answer with a list of names, and most of the names are already dead."},"lost_jedi":{"id":"lost_jedi","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE LOST ONES","text":"When the Order was hunted to ash, its survivors scattered into the outer worlds. They learned to hide their sabers beneath cloaks and their names beneath false ones. A few still gather in secret, teaching the young what the Temple once taught openly."},"jedi_ranks":{"id":"jedi_ranks","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE JEDI RANKS","text":"An Initiate is a child in the Temple's care. A Padawan is chosen by a Knight or Master to be trained. A Knight has passed the trials, may walk alone, and may take an apprentice. A Master has trained a Knight or proven wisdom beyond doubt."},"jedi_battlemaster":{"id":"jedi_battlemaster","cat":"FACTION","title":"BATTLEMASTER","text":"The Order's chief lightsaber instructor. Only one holds the title at a time, chosen by the High Council to lead the academy's combat training. It is a teaching post, not a rank, and it carries the weight of every student who fell beneath the teacher's eye."},"sith_remnants":{"id":"sith_remnants","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE SITH REMNANTS","text":"The Sith empire broke into warring lords and then into ash. What remains is scattered: a cult in one ruin, a tomb-keeper in another, relic hunters who whisper of a master never found. They share no banner. They share a hunger."},"triumvirate_assassins":{"id":"triumvirate_assassins","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE MASKLESS","text":"The Triumvirate's assassins were trained to kill Jedi in their sleep and their sanctuaries. Now masterless, they sell their blades to whoever can pay. Some still wear the cowl. Others burned it and kept only the skill. Ask a cowl's wearer for his master's name, and he will not answer."},"czerka_corp":{"id":"czerka_corp","cat":"FACTION","title":"CZERKA CORPORATION","text":"Czerka mines the rock, builds the droids, and sells whatever turns a profit. Its contracts are signed in a dozen tongues and honored only when enforced. Scavengers call its surplus crates a gift. The Corporation calls it liability relief."},"hutt_clans":{"id":"hutt_clans","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE HUTT CLANS","text":"On Hutta the clans trade in debts, flesh, and favors. The Cartel binds them loosely, and each clan guards its holdings more fiercely than any treaty. Most who serve them never see daylight. Their pits run beneath the cantinas where the bets are placed."},"trandoshan_hunters":{"id":"trandoshan_hunters","cat":"FACTION","title":"TRANDOSHAN HUNTERS","text":"The Trandoshans reckon every life in points, awarded by the Scorekeeper for each kill. They take prisoners alive whenever they can, because a living trophy is worth more than a corpse. Their honor is rigid, and once a word is given it becomes law."},"bounty_hunters":{"id":"bounty_hunters","cat":"FACTION","title":"CONTRACT HUNTERS","text":"No guild holds them to account. A hunter takes a name, a price, and a deadline, then vanishes into the cantinas until the job is done. Many carry old Republic blasters and borrowed armor. The best mark their hulls with a single sigil and never explain it."},"mandalorian_remnant":{"id":"mandalorian_remnant","cat":"FACTION","title":"THE MANDALORIAN REMNANT","text":"Before the wars, Dxun was a clan stronghold, its bunkers cut deep into the rock. The clans scattered when their war-leader fell. A few stubborn kin still camp in the ruins, rebuilding their war-ways one salvaged plate at a time."},"mandalorian_wars":{"id":"mandalorian_wars","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE MANDALORIAN WARS","text":"For three bitter years the clans of Mandalore burned their way through Republic space. Their warriors wore armor that shrugged off blaster fire and fought with a fury the Republic had not seen since the old Sith wars. The war ended in fire above Malachor."},"malachor_v":{"id":"malachor_v","cat":"HISTORY","title":"MALACHOR V","text":"A moon scarred by a weapon too terrible to name. Those who survived its last battle heard something tear through the Force, a silence that did not lift. Malachor is said to hold a wound still. Those who walk its ruins come back changed, or they do not come back."},"jedi_civil_war":{"id":"jedi_civil_war","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE JEDI CIVIL WAR","text":"Brothers and sisters of the Order turned their sabers on one another. Temples burned, and the Council's trust rotted from within. The war ended in a shattered fleet and a galaxy that no longer believed the Jedi stood above politics."},"first_purge":{"id":"first_purge","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE PURGE","text":"For three years the Sith hunted every Jedi who could be found. Assassins struck in temples and cantinas alike, and whole worlds were drained searching for one hidden student. The survivors learned the value of silence, and they have not forgotten the names of the dead."},"the_three":{"id":"the_three","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE THREE","text":"Three Sith ruled from a fortress above Malachor. Their war was waged on the Force itself as much as on the Jedi. Their rivalry proved as deadly as their campaign, and the galaxy learned the cost of their victories in cold graves and empty temples."},"dxun_wars":{"id":"dxun_wars","cat":"HISTORY","title":"DXUN IN THE WARS","text":"A jungle moon of Onderon, thick with beasts that hunt in packs. Mandalorian armies once dug in here, and their bunkers still breathe damp air. Old dark-side residue clings to the trees. The locals call it the demon moon and never go there after dark."},"nadd_tomb":{"id":"nadd_tomb","cat":"HISTORY","title":"TOMB OF FREEDON NADD","text":"A black iron spire on a hilltop, raised after the last of a dead Sith lord's worshippers were put down. No vine has ever touched it. Its locked chambers hold scrolls and parasites that feed on the living. Those who enter seldom leave with their minds intact."},"raxus_prime":{"id":"raxus_prime","cat":"HISTORY","title":"RAXUS PRIME","text":"A world choked with factories and toxic lakes, so crowded with wreckage that its people call it the galaxy's refuse pit. Old war machines sprout from the sludge like weeds. Deep beneath the wreckage, an older engine hums to itself, waiting for someone clever enough to dig."},"hutta_pits":{"id":"hutta_pits","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE PITS OF HUTTA","text":"The Hutt homeworld, where slaves are a crop and the pits are a lottery. The arena behind the cantina pays in bets and blood. Losers are tallied, winners are branded with the count of their victories. The galaxy calls Hutta a backwater. Those born there call it a cage."},"darth_title":{"id":"darth_title","cat":"FORCE","title":"DARTH","text":"The old word means dark lord, and many wore it before any rule governed the wearing. A Sith takes it when power has made the claim true. The galaxy respects a title only after the blood has been spilled to earn it, and then fears it."},"force_wound":{"id":"force_wound","cat":"FORCE","title":"A WOUND IN THE FORCE","text":"Some Jedi say the Force flows through all living things. The Sith in broken temples say it has been wounded, and that the wound spreads like rot. Those who touch it feel a silence that does not end. Ask a survivor of Malachor what she heard, and she will not finish."},"seeing_cracks":{"id":"seeing_cracks","cat":"FORCE","title":"SEEING THE CRACKS","text":"Every ship, mind, and bond has flaws. A trained eye sees the strain in a hull, the fear in a voice, the shame beneath a vow. The Force shows these cracks to the patient. Strike there, and the thing breaks for you."},"quiet_presence":{"id":"quiet_presence","cat":"FORCE","title":"QUIET IN THE FORCE","text":"A skilled presence can hide inside the Force. Stillness blends it into the ambient flow, and distraction lures a searching mind away. The best hunters vanish into a crowd, leaving only a faint absence that the sharpest senses might notice."},"sith_alchemy":{"id":"sith_alchemy","cat":"FORCE","title":"SITH ALCHEMY","text":"Dark rituals can harden a blade, bind an enchantment into a robe, or wake a relic's sleeping power. The practice is ugly and imprecise. Each success is paid for in pain, and most failures are found in the wreckage of the alchemist's own workshop."},"holocrons":{"id":"holocrons","cat":"FORCE","title":"HOLOCRONS","text":"Crystal memory-engines that hold the teachings of masters and seal them against the unworthy. A holocron may speak, plead, or lie. Its locks answer to the bearer's intent, and its voice remembers the one who recorded it long after that one is dead."},"kyber_crystal":{"id":"kyber_crystal","cat":"FORCE","title":"KYBER","text":"The crystal at the heart of every lightsaber. Its color answers to the hand that holds it. Pure kyber sings bright for the light, but bends and blackens under dark hands. Those who cut crystals say the stone remembers the first voice that touched it."},"tainted_kyber":{"id":"tainted_kyber","cat":"FORCE","title":"TAINTED KYBER","text":"Crystals grown or corrupted in the dark. Their color is wrong, a red that bleeds at the edges. They answer rage with a surge of power and repay it with corruption that creeps into the bearer's hand. Synthetic crystals copy the look, but not the cost."},"assassin_databank":{"id":"assassin_databank","cat":"TECH","title":"ASSASSIN DATABANK","text":"A Czerka-pattern droid mind built to study enemies. It records every stance, flinch, and hesitation. Its voice is dry and its loyalty conditional. Its advice is always about patterns: Jedi are creatures of ritual, it says, and ritual can be broken."},"stealth_courier":{"id":"stealth_courier","cat":"TECH","title":"STEALTH COURIER","text":"A slender courier hull with a cloak that swallows starlight. Its engines are quiet, its sensors cheap, and its hold smells of burnt coolant. Smugglers prize it because no patrol logs its passage. Its name changes with every owner, and so does its paint."},"cr90_corvette":{"id":"cr90_corvette","cat":"TECH","title":"CR90 CORVETTE","text":"An old Republic workhorse, its bow scarred by a hundred boarding actions. The Judicial Forces retired it to the scrapyards, and then scavengers bought it cheap. Its turbolasers still fire, though the power couplings grumble. It is slow, ugly, and very hard to kill."},"republic_carbine":{"id":"republic_carbine","cat":"TECH","title":"REPUBLIC CARBINE","text":"A blaster carbine issued by the thousand to Republic infantry. It is heavy, accurate, and easy to strip in the dark. Its power cell fits a dozen civilian blasters. Soldiers say it kicks like a mule and never jams, the only praise a soldier gives a weapon."},"combat_plate":{"id":"combat_plate","cat":"TECH","title":"COMBAT PLATE","text":"Layers of composite plate over a flexible weave. It stops a blaster bolt at close range and softens a vibroblade's bite. It is loud when worn, and its seams wear through in one bad season. Mercenaries strip it and sell the plates separately."},"dxun_moon":{"id":"dxun_moon","cat":"PLACE","title":"Dxun, the Demon Moon","text":"Largest of the four moons turning around Onderon, Dxun wears its jungle like a shroud. Storms roll in without warning, and the things beneath the canopy have never needed a reason to hunt. Settlers who came for timber stayed as bones. Those who came for the Sith stayed longer than they meant to."},"dxun_jungle":{"id":"dxun_jungle","cat":"PLACE","title":"The Green Dark","text":"Light reaches the forest floor only in fractured shafts. Above, drexl wheel through ferns the height of towers. Below, mud swallows boots and root-arches drip with rot. The jungle is not hostile by intent. It is simply hungry, and it has grown hungrier since the Dark Lords came to feed on its nexus."},"freedon_nadd_tomb":{"id":"freedon_nadd_tomb","cat":"PLACE","title":"The Black Spire","text":"The tomb of Freedon Nadd stands alone on a hill above the valley, a spire of black Mandalorian iron that no vine has touched in four thousand years. A broad landing pad juts from its base. Scholars call its bare stone impossible. Those who have stood at its breach say the silence is listening."},"mandalorian_ruins_dxun":{"id":"mandalorian_ruins_dxun","cat":"PLACE","title":"Mandalorian Ruins","text":"Here the Mandalorians held Dxun until Revan's assault broke their line. Bunkers sag into the mud and craters hold black water. Rusted wire hangs in the ferns, and under the moss, minefields still wait. The Guard Captain who keeps this camp has forgotten why he stays. He only knows the ground is his."},"jungle_tomb":{"id":"jungle_tomb","cat":"PLACE","title":"The Jungle Tomb","text":"A lesser tomb hides among the roots, its door ringed by mines and perimeter sensors that wake at the slightest disturbance. Its old builders wanted no grave robbers. The priests who kept it sealed their secrets behind sensor codes, and the codes still answer to anyone who knows how to ask."},"snare_clearing":{"id":"snare_clearing","cat":"PLACE","title":"The Snare Clearing","text":"A ship cannot come quietly to the Warren, so none do. The landing clearing is rigged with snares and crude mines. Listening devices hang in the canopy and scavenged turrets sleep in their pits. Anything that drops through the haze trips an alarm before its engines have cooled."},"iziz_city":{"id":"iziz_city","cat":"PLACE","title":"Iziz","text":"Iziz rises behind massive walls, angular and proud, its brown facades capped with blue roofs and crowned by pyramid temples. The city was built to keep the jungle out. The gate is a bridge under turret fire and ray shields, and every citizen knows the beasts beyond the wall are only waiting."},"iziz_palace":{"id":"iziz_palace","cat":"PLACE","title":"The Royal Palace","text":"The palace stands on a hill over Iziz, reached by a stone-and-steel ramp that climbs from the starport to the southern gates. Its throne room was moved to the rear in later years, but the hill remembers the old tyrant. Ray shields hum across the stairs, and the turrets are polished for every new queen."},"onderon_planet":{"id":"onderon_planet","cat":"PLACE","title":"Onderon","text":"Onderon is a temperate world of green plains and walled cities, a place that might have been peaceful if the moon in its sky did not bring the beasts. Its people fortified every town against Dxun's hunters, and its royal houses were built of the same stone and the same fear."},"warren_of_lesser_tombs":{"id":"warren_of_lesser_tombs","cat":"PLACE","title":"The Warren","text":"Beneath the roots of an ancient temple, Rathatri made his home. Not the grand tomb of Nadd, but the scrap-lined crypts above it, where cracked statues watch and burial niches hold sleeping killers. He chose it for its hidden door, its narrow throats and the dark tricks still whispering in its walls."},"cannok":{"id":"cannok","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Cannok","text":"The cannok runs in bristling swarms through the undergrowth, breeding faster than the jungle can eat them. Alone, one is a nuisance. In a crowd of thirty, a cannok will swallow whatever fits in its jaws, and sometimes what does not. Zakkegs grow fat on them, and so do the scavengers who follow the zakkegs."},"maalraa":{"id":"maalraa","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Maalraa","text":"The maalraa stalks like a cougar and hunts like a ghost. It waits in the canopy for a wounded traveler to stumble past, then drops with a silent crash of leaves. Its claws can open armor seams. Those who survive the first leap rarely see a second, and the jungle keeps quiet about it."},"boma":{"id":"boma","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Boma","text":"The boma is a slow mountain of armored flesh, but it is not slow when its territory is breached. Mandalorians learned to fear its charge, and zakkegs learned to hunt its young. A tamed boma carries its rider through the storms like a living fortress, and its loyalty lasts only as long as the will that holds its reins."},"zakkeg":{"id":"zakkeg","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Zakkeg","text":"The zakkeg is the jungle's apex: a brown, thick-hided reptile with talons wider than a hand. It guards its territory like a sentry at a gate and does not share the ground. A zakkeg's ear is the proof of a kill, and its roar ends arguments among the scavengers."},"drexl":{"id":"drexl","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Drexl","text":"The drexl is a winged predator of purple scale, its males spanning twenty meters from tip to tip. Onderon's Beast Riders trained them as mounts, and a rider who holds the reins can cross the valley faster than any speeder. Bane once flew one from Dxun to Onderon, and few riders live to dismount."},"orbalisk":{"id":"orbalisk","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Orbalisk","text":"The orbalisk waits dormant in the caves, a cluster of dark shells like stones, until a host wanders close. Then it wakes. Thousands of tiny teeth grip the skin, and the thing spreads, smothering breath and light alike. Its shell can turn a lightsaber aside, and Nadd and Bane both wore it as armor."},"predatory_flora":{"id":"predatory_flora","cat":"CREATURE","title":"Hunger Vines","text":"Some of Dxun's plants learned to hunt when the dark side seeped into the soil. Their vines coil around anything warm, and their blossoms breathe a sweet mist that dulls the victim. Under Nadd's influence the jungle became a predator. Never walk beneath a flower on Dxun."},"freedon_nadd_holocron":{"id":"freedon_nadd_holocron","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"Holocron of Freedon Nadd","text":"Nadd's holocron waits in the deepest chamber of his tomb, its facets dulled by four thousand years of stillness. Darth Bane found it and learned from its voice how to make the orbalisk armor. Whoever wakes it hears the old tyrant's promise of power first, and only later the price."},"orbalisk_armor":{"id":"orbalisk_armor","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"Orbalisk Armor","text":"Plates of living-dark shell, grown and fitted to the body, that keep orbalisks from the face, hands and feet. Only Nadd and Bane are known to have worn it. The armor brings strength and healing, but it blinds the wearer to stealth and makes every shadow loud. Some say the shell can turn a blade aside."},"nadd_short_lightsaber":{"id":"nadd_short_lightsaber","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"Nadd's Short Lightsaber","text":"In the sarcophagus at the back of the ritual chamber lies the short saber of Freedon Nadd, its hilt a black spine of Mandalorian iron. Its blade once burned a dull crimson. Whoever claims it is said to hear the old tyrant laughing as the crystal hums."},"mandalorian_iron":{"id":"mandalorian_iron","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"Mandalorian Iron","text":"Smelted by hands that feared the Republic, Mandalorian iron resists blasters, fire and time. Nadd's tomb is built from it, and the wrecks in the Mandalorian ruins bear its scars. Smiths who learned to work it say the metal remembers every blow and refuses to forget the one that broke it."},"ward_stone":{"id":"ward_stone","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"Ward Stone","text":"Sith ward stones ring the old temples, humming with power their makers understood and their successors only half remember. Rathatri has learned to coax them into snare fields and bursts of chaotic force, but never without risk. A ward that misfires can burn the hand that woke it, or the whole chamber around it."},"nadd_dynasty":{"id":"nadd_dynasty","cat":"HISTORY","title":"Nadd's Dynasty","text":"Freedon Nadd killed his master, Naga Sadow, and made himself tyrant of Iziz, bending the court to the dark side. He banished criminals beyond the walls to die in the jungle. Many did not die. They tamed the beasts, and the dynasty that thought it had buried its enemies found them waiting at the gates."},"naga_sadow_fall":{"id":"naga_sadow_fall","cat":"HISTORY","title":"The Death of Naga Sadow","text":"Naga Sadow taught Freedon Nadd the Sith arts, and Nadd repaid him with a blade. The apprentice carried his murdered master's lessons to Onderon and built a throne from them. Sadow's teachings were the reason Nadd was dangerous, and his killing was the reason Onderon bled."},"beast_riders":{"id":"beast_riders","cat":"HISTORY","title":"The Beast Riders","text":"Exiled to the jungle, the criminals of Onderon learned to speak with the beasts. They rode drexl across the sky and bomas across the plains. When the queen's soldiers hunted them, the Beast Riders answered. A raid took Princess Galia, and the Jedi who came to save her found the Kira fortress and the boma that led them there."},"arca_jeth_entombment":{"id":"arca_jeth_entombment","cat":"HISTORY","title":"The Second Tomb","text":"After Nadd's worshippers were destroyed in 3998 BBY, Jedi Master Arca Jeth moved the Dark Lord's tomb from its cavern beneath the palace of Iziz to the jungle moon Dxun. Nadd lies there with his queen, Amanoa, and his king, Ommin. The new tomb was built to contain his remains and the dark side that still clung to them."},"exar_kun_breach":{"id":"exar_kun_breach","cat":"HISTORY","title":"Exar Kun's Breach","text":"Exar Kun came to the tomb in search of forbidden knowledge and cut a wound in its outer wall with his lightsaber. The iron of the wall is nearly unbreakable, yet he cut through it. Scholars still argue whether he came a year after sealing or much later. The breach is still open, and it still smells of smoke."},"mandalorian_wars_dxun":{"id":"mandalorian_wars_dxun","cat":"HISTORY","title":"The Battle of Dxun","text":"The Mandalorians made Dxun a fleet command post and sowed its valleys with mines, turrets and traps for decades. When Revan's armies came, the jungle fought beside the defenders. Meetra Surik's line charged across a minefield and lost most of its soldiers. The Republic lost ten for every Mandalorian, the Mandalorians said. The craters still answer."},"bane_dxun":{"id":"bane_dxun","cat":"HISTORY","title":"Bane in the Tomb","text":"Darth Bane came to the tomb of Freedon Nadd and found what the Dark Lord had left behind: a holocron and a nest of orbalisks. He took both, and the armor he made from the shells changed him. What one master leaves to rot, the next master takes up. He took a drexl as well, and flew it to Onderon."},"vaklu_revolt":{"id":"vaklu_revolt","cat":"HISTORY","title":"Vaklu's Revolt","text":"General Vaklu, cousin to Queen Talia, wanted Onderon free of the Republic, and he had found friends among the Sith. He declared martial law in Iziz and sent his soldiers against the palace to finish his cousin. He failed and was imprisoned. The Sith had bargained with him for the tomb of Nadd."},"nihilus_dxun_3951":{"id":"nihilus_dxun_3951","cat":"HISTORY","title":"The Dark Lord's Last Vigil","text":"In 3951 BBY the loyalists of Darth Nihilus held the tomb of Freedon Nadd, and Onderon's general had promised them the road. They built their power in the spire's shadow until Meetra Surik's companions came up through the jungle and broke them at its doors. The valley has been quiet since, though nothing living there is at peace."},"starving_beast":{"id":"starving_beast","cat":"ORDER","title":"THE STARVING BEAST","text":"The first trial has no teacher. Recruits are left in the deep jungle with a knife, a day's water and one instruction: come back to the temple. Dxun does the rest. Those who return have learned the only lesson that matters here. Everything that lives is either hunting or being hunted, and hesitation decides which."},"traya":{"id":"traya","cat":"FORCE","title":"THE HOLOCRON OF TRAYA","text":"A pyramid of cracked crystal that wakes in a ghost of grey robes and a voice like a blade drawn slowly. She calls herself Traya, and sometimes Kreia, and she does not teach. She asks questions until the answers cut. Every lesson she gives has a price, and she never says what it is until it has been paid."},"heat":{"id":"heat","cat":"ORDER","title":"THE RUMOR","text":"A Sith Lord who is seen is a Sith Lord who is hunted. Every witness, every holo-recording, every hunter who walks away alive is a thread back to Dxun. Pull enough threads and the Republic sends commandos, then Jedi, then the Battlemaster himself. Silence the rumor, or be ready to meet what it brings."},"place_hutta_pits":{"id":"place_hutta_pits","cat":"PLACE","title":"HUTTA: THE PIT BEHIND THE CANTINA","text":"Behind the cantina's grease-lit door lies a ring of stone where the crowd roars for blood. Nobody here has a name. A number is chalked on the gate, a wager is scrawled beside it, and the drainage sluice floods the ring when the losers are still breathing."},"place_nal_hutta_marsh":{"id":"place_nal_hutta_marsh","cat":"PLACE","title":"NAL HUTTA: THE HUTT MARSH","text":"Greasy rain falls on the marsh the Hutts claim as their seat. Mud swallows the roads, and the oldest clans hold court on raised causeways, where the wealthy never have to step in the water they sell."},"place_nar_shaddaa":{"id":"place_nar_shaddaa","cat":"PLACE","title":"NAR SHADDAA: THE SMUGGLERS' MOON","text":"Stacked thousands of levels high, the Smugglers' Moon never sees the sun. Neon bleeds through the lattice, cargo swings overhead, and every fence on the Promenade keeps a ledger. The Exchange sells anything, and it remembers exactly who owes it."},"place_zx34_silent_sanctum":{"id":"place_zx34_silent_sanctum","cat":"PLACE","title":"ZX34: THE SILENT SANCTUM","text":"A small grey moon hangs beneath a banded giant the locals call the Veil. Carved into a cliff of black basalt is a hall where the Force goes quiet. Step inside and your presence leaves an absence, a hole in the world that others can feel."},"place_ambria_glass":{"id":"place_ambria_glass","cat":"PLACE","title":"AMBRIA: THE GLASS WASTES","text":"Dunes of black sand roll toward a horizon of ochre dust. Where two rival Sith once fought, the desert fused into mirror-smooth lakes of obsidian. Beneath the storm a tall black obelisk still stands, its cracks glowing like a wound that never closed."},"place_raxus_prime_heap":{"id":"place_raxus_prime_heap","cat":"PLACE","title":"RAXUS PRIME: THE HEAP","text":"Once a capital of the Kingdom of Cron, this world now drowns in its own waste. Smog hangs over buried towers and rusted hulls, and acid pools steam in the hollows. Scavengers climb the wreckage of a war four thousand years dead."},"place_reaper_ring":{"id":"place_reaper_ring","cat":"PLACE","title":"THE REAPER RING","text":"A crater of glassy slag marks where the Dark Reaper fell. Hundreds of soldiers died in a single flash, and the heap has tried to forget them ever since. On windless nights the ring is silent, but the dead still march toward its center."},"place_krayiss_ii_temple":{"id":"place_krayiss_ii_temple","cat":"PLACE","title":"KRAYISS II: THE LIBRARY-TEMPLE","text":"Sith sorcerers once came here to read in silence, and the temple still keeps their discipline. Buried beneath the crags, its halls answer only the worthy. The obelisk above is the only part left standing, and the spirits within have never forgiven the Jedi who came knocking."},"place_stygian_caldera":{"id":"place_stygian_caldera","cat":"PLACE","title":"THE STYGIAN CALDERA","text":"Violet nebula light pours over basalt crags, and sulfur rises on the wind from vents below. In the Sith Worlds at the edge of the caldera, the stars seem to lean closer, as if listening for a voice that stopped speaking long ago."},"place_lenico_ash_plains":{"id":"place_lenico_ash_plains","cat":"PLACE","title":"LENICO IV: THE ASH PLAINS","text":"Ash drifts over fused-glass pans where a small tribe of thin Ortolans once lived. Aurora curtains ripple across the sky with no source. Pirates avoid the plains, and the few who wander there return quiet, unable to say what they saw."},"place_lenico_colony_blue":{"id":"place_lenico_colony_blue","cat":"PLACE","title":"LENICO COLONY BLUE","text":"The colony station hangs over the Lenico system like a tooth in an open mouth. Its domes were abandoned in a hurry. The hangars still hold cargo, and the final logs stop mid-sentence. The crews who fled took only what they could carry and never spoke of the ash."},"artifact_tainted_kyber":{"id":"artifact_tainted_kyber","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"TAINTED KYBER CRYSTAL","text":"A kyber crystal, dark as spilled ink, that remembers the duel that clouded it. Hold it, and rage rises through your bones like a tide. Every surge feels like strength. The crystal never mentions the cost, and it always, always asks which of the rivals you would have stabbed."},"artifact_legacy_of_betrayal":{"id":"artifact_legacy_of_betrayal","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"LEGACY OF BETRAYAL","text":"A data-slate account written by one of two Sith acolytes who turned on their master. Its margins hold notes and underlined phrases, and one word is scratched out: trust. Milian kept it near her bed as a warning. Whoever reads it closely learns exactly where a master bleeds."},"artifact_ritual_of_binding":{"id":"artifact_ritual_of_binding","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"FRAGMENT OF THE RITUAL OF BINDING","text":"A tablet of black stone, half its glyphs gone, describes how a living will is bent into servitude. The rite demands a circle, a heartbeat of focus, and a creature willing to be held. The last line warns that the bound beast will remember the hand that tamed it."},"artifact_mask_of_despair":{"id":"artifact_mask_of_despair","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"MASK OF DESPAIR","text":"A pale mask of bone and resin, its eye-holes filled with grey glass. Those who wear it see their own failures walking beside them. Jedi seekers lose the scent of their quarry while it is worn, and the mask never grows heavier, though the wearer's heart does."},"artifact_foundry_databank":{"id":"artifact_foundry_databank","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"FOUNDRY DATABANK","text":"A Sith-tuned droid core still humming with tactical routines. Its voice is dry and certain. It notes that Jedi rely on patterns, and that patterns can be broken. Its banks hold the war-droid lines of the Great Sith War, the marching orders, and the flaws in every lightsaber form."},"artifact_sith_amulet":{"id":"artifact_sith_amulet","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"SITH AMULET","text":"A thumb-sized disc of dull black metal, sold on the Promenade with a grin and a warning. Its inscription is worn smooth by a hundred hands, each one paying too much. The amulet is cheap as a lie, and its power is only as strong as the debt its buyer carries."},"artifact_bone_hilt":{"id":"artifact_bone_hilt","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"PIT BEAST BONE HILT","text":"The grip of Rathatri's first lightsaber, carved from the jaw of the beast he killed in the pit. The bone is still stained brown, and a hairline crack runs along it like a memory the bone refuses to forget. Every wielder who ever held it knew where it came from."},"artifact_obelisk_shard":{"id":"artifact_obelisk_shard","cat":"ARTIFACT","title":"OBELISK SHARD","text":"A fragment of black glass chipped from the Ambrian obelisk, cold even in the desert heat. Its surface reflects a duel that never happened in this light. Thon once caged the sorcerer's power in a single spot. This shard is proof the cage has been opened, and that someone was holding the key."},"history_evocii_displacement":{"id":"history_evocii_displacement","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE EVOCII'S FALL","text":"Some fifteen thousand years before this age, the Hutts drove the Evocii from their world onto a grey moon. The Evocii built the docks and spaceports that still hold the Smugglers' Moon together, then were enslaved for their labor. Their names were lost in the grind."},"history_sacred_sith_worlds":{"id":"history_sacred_sith_worlds","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE FIVE SACRED WORLDS","text":"Before the Sith scattered, five worlds were holy to them. Krayiss II was the most isolated, a library-temple of silent study colonized before the fourteenth millennium BBY. When the caldera swallowed it, only the obelisk stayed above ground, a finger raised in warning to anyone who would dig."},"history_vara_nreem":{"id":"history_vara_nreem","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE DEATH OF VARA NREEM","text":"Forty-nine years before this age, a Jedi named Vara Nreem walked into the sacred library-temple of Krayiss II. The spirits within weighed her and found her unworthy. Her body was never recovered from the glyph halls, and the obelisk still whispers her name to the storm."},"history_smog_of_cron":{"id":"history_smog_of_cron","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE SMOG OF CRON","text":"By eleven hundred years before this age, the factories of Raxus Prime had choked the capitals of the Kingdom of Cron. Smog rolled over the towers, the waste swallowed the streets, and the great world became a junkyard that nobody bothered to clean."},"history_dark_reaper":{"id":"history_dark_reaper","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE DARK REAPER AT RAXUS","text":"In the Great Sith War, the Sith lord Ulic Qel-Droma unleashed the Dark Reaper over Raxus Prime. Hundreds of Republic soldiers died in a single flash, and their dying minds turned the ground into a field of echoes. The scorched crater is still called the Reaper Ring."},"history_ortolan_massacre":{"id":"history_ortolan_massacre","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE ORTOLANS OF THE ASH PLAINS","text":"The tribe on the Ash Plains was thin as bone and deep in the old rites. A Sith Emperor wanted those rites to carry his mind into new bodies. He sent his apprentice Exal Kressh to learn them, and when she had them, he ordered the village slain. She obeyed, then swore to bring him down."},"history_thon_ambria":{"id":"history_thon_ambria","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THON AND THE CAGED FIRE","text":"A Sith sorceress raised an obelisk on Ambria and tried to command the whole planet through its ritual. The power turned on her and killed her. The Jedi Master Thon came after, sealing the influence within one spot and training apprentices in the desert heat until the Great Sith War called him away."},"history_tho_natu_990":{"id":"history_tho_natu_990","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE HUNT OF 990 BBY","text":"A Jedi strike team came to Ambria to take the last known Sith Lord. In the glass wastes they met Darovit, a cousin of Darth Zannah, driven mad by her sorcery. Tho'natu cut him down, believing him to be the prize. The wrong man died on the glass that day."},"history_goto_exchange":{"id":"history_goto_exchange","cat":"HISTORY","title":"GOTO AND THE EXCHANGE","text":"When the Exchange ruled the Smugglers' Moon, its boss was a droid that never left its office. Goto spoke through a hologram and collected on debts. Meetra Surik later cut down two of its crime lords, but the lower levels still whisper its name when a deal goes sour."},"history_glass_war":{"id":"history_glass_war","cat":"HISTORY","title":"THE GLASS WAR","text":"Two fallen Jedi, once allies, turned their war on each other over the obelisk that Thon once caged. It lasted less than a season. Their armies fused the dunes into mirrors with lightning and fire, and both died in the glass. The obelisk remains, and the rival whose name was struck from every record is still said to walk the glass at night."}},"quotes":["A leash is only a rope until someone holds the other end. - Sith proverb","Pain is a door. Walk through it, or stay on the hinges. - Milian, to her apprentice","The strong do not ask. The strong take, and remember. - Sith proverb","Fear is a current. Learn to swim in it, or drown. - Sith saying","Empires are built on the bones of the last empire. - Sith proverb","Names are for the living. Titles are for the feared. - Sith proverb","A rumor cannot be killed. It can only be outlived. - Dxun saying","The dark side does not corrupt. It reveals what you were hiding. - Sith proverb","The Scorekeeper forgets nothing, and forgives only in the ledger. - Trandoshan saying","Prey runs. The hunter remembers the run. - Trandoshan saying","A life spared is a debt written in scale. - Trandoshan proverb","Teeth are old. Patience is older. - Trandoshan saying","The strong tally kills. The wise tally debts. - Trandoshan saying","A kill unrecorded is a hunt wasted. - Trandoshan saying","Mud keeps the footprints of the careless. - Trandoshan saying","The Scorekeeper's book has no last page. - Trandoshan saying","A debt is a leash made of credits. - Hutt proverb","Never bet against a Hutt's patience. It is older than your bloodline. - Hutt proverb","Let others fight. Let others bleed. Let me collect. - Hutt proverb","The arena pays for courage. The house pays for everything else. - Pit-master Tohgrun Vak","What is owed is never forgotten, only postponed. - Hutt proverb","A hungry pit makes brighter champions. - Pit-master Tohgrun Vak","The crowd roars for the wounded. The house takes the wager. - Hutt proverb","Every investment has a short lifespan. Plan accordingly. - Hutt proverb","Peace is not the absence of struggle, but mastery of it. - Aiden Kyros","There is no passion, there is serenity. - Jedi Code","Breathe. The Force is patient, even when we are not. - Jedi proverb","A blade drawn in anger cuts its owner first. - Jedi saying","We were broken once. We remember the breaking. - Order of the Rebuild","One Jedi's light can outlast a thousand Sith empires. - Jedi saying","The dark does not announce itself. It waits in the quiet. - Jedi warning","Listen before you strike. The enemy always whispers first. - Aiden Kyros","Do not mistake brutality for the artistry of a true warrior. - Darth Traya","Seek not just relics or Force techniques, but understanding. - Darth Traya","Master the darkness swirling within you. Meditate not on peace, but on control. - Darth Traya","Let your hatred become a scalpel you wield, not a storm that consumes you. - Darth Traya","It was but a title, as meaningless as countless others the galaxy forgets. - Darth Traya","Every failing is a lesson to be turned against their kind. - Darth Traya","Do you understand the difference between using the dark side and being consumed by it? - Darth Traya","Darth Traya was the mask I wore to confront the Jedi. - Darth Traya"],"barks":{"commando":["Your hunt ends at the Republic perimeter, Sith.","Hold fire! I want him breathing for the tribunal.","Shields up! Target is a Sith. Repeat, Sith.","Smile for the holo, Sith. Your face is on a warrant.","The Republic sends its regards. Mostly through our rifles.","Paperwork says you're dead. Let's make it official.","No more rumors. Just a body for the slab.","We don't negotiate with dark-side trash.","Form on me! Crossfire on the bridge!","Move up, cover the left flank!","You're a rumor with a pulse. Let's fix that.","Lay down your blade. Republic law applies.","This is Republic militia. Surrender or be cleared.","Target spotted, north ruin. Converge!","Fire discipline! Don't waste the cells!","Your temple's sealed. Your tomb's ours now.","We're not cutting you down clean. Hold still.","Sergeant says you're worth a medal. Pity it's posthumous.","Eyes on the Sith. Ignore the screaming. Keep firing.","We don't retreat, Sith. We advance.","Medic! I'm hit! Left side!","Armor's cracked. I'm still on my feet.","Shield's down! Get me behind the crate!","Rifle's cooked. Switching to sidearm!","Tell my squad I held the bridge.","Kriff, that burned. Keep firing!","Pull me back! Don't leave me on the stone!","Ow. Ow. Ow. Okay, I'm up.","Sarge, I'm bleeding out here!","That Force push threw me into the wall.","Armor's holding. Mostly. Keep moving!","Hand's numb. Switching grips.","Still breathing, still firing!","Visor's fogged! Clear it, somebody!","Good hit, Sith. I'll remember that.","Eyes open. Sector clear. Mostly.","Anybody else hear drums in the trees?","Count your magazines before you count kills.","Quiet out here. Too quiet.","Check the south tomb. Sith love tombs.","Clear the next room, then clear it again.","Take the ledge. Watch the stair.","Comm check. Sound off, one by one.","Keep the line tight, shoulder to shoulder.","Rumors don't bleed. Remember that when you aim.","Hold position. Wait for the Jedi signal.","This moon eats boots. Watch your footing.","Rations cold. Mission colder. Stay sharp.","Who sent a warrant for a Sith? Nice work.","Sergeant says we stay till the ritual's broken.","Flank! Two on the causeway!","Grenade out! Get down!","Reloading! Cover me!","Shield wall forming! Hold!","Target retreating north! Pursue!","Plasma charge primed! Clear!","Medic, reposition to the east steps!","Heavy in the ruins! Use the crates!","Crossfire! Keep the lane open!","Sith on the ridge! Fire!"],"bhunter":["Price just went up, Sith. Dead or breathing.","Bounty's posted. I'm collecting. Hold still.","Credits don't care who killed you, friend.","Nice rumor. Shame it's about to be a corpse.","Easy money, slow way. Let's make it quick.","Your head's worth more than your temple, Sith.","I've killed bigger rumors before breakfast.","Whip's out. Time to fetch the prize.","Jet's warm. Watch me come down on you.","Nobody hires me to be merciful.","Ooh, shiny saber. I'll take it for scrap.","Bounty's posted in four systems. Lucky you.","I'll bring your ears in a box. Standard fee.","Fifty for your head. A hundred for the hilt.","Hold position, Sith. Let me work.","Dead Sith don't argue about the fee.","Pay me now, or pay the next one.","Your temple's a lot of bones for one tomb.","Easy bounty, hard bounty. Same paycheck.","Come out, come out, Sith. Your fee is waiting.","Ow! Armor's a joke, I swear!","That whip... my shoulder's gone!","My jet's sparking, dang it!","Who taught you to hit like that?","Okay, okay. Bounty's a bad idea.","I'm bleeding for scrap, Sith!","Fast for a rumor. Rough, rough.","Medkit! Somebody sign for it!","That's cutting my fee in half!","Argh! My jetpack's on fire!","Fine. I'll retreat and bill you later.","My ribs. My pride. Mostly my ribs.","That's a clean shot. Respect.","Still standing, Sith. Still standing!","Hurts! Next round's on me, though.","Dry rain, wet jungle, cold dinner. Standard.","Check the board again. Maybe he's worth more.","Nobody pays for patience. Move, friend.","Contract says alive preferred. Bonus for alive.","Jet fuel's expensive. Make the fight count.","Tracker's blinking. He's in the trees.","This sector smells like a bad contract.","Every Sith has a price. Find the number.","Snare's set. Walk into it, please.","Ask the Hutts what they'd pay for his ears.","Breathe. Count the credits. Breathe again.","Got a scent. Smells like a lie.","Paid by the hour, dead by the minute.","Rumors pay, rumors die. Let's get paid.","I'll wait. Waiting is also a job.","Flanking left! Keep him in the open!","Jet dash incoming! Watch the ground!","Whip out! Stay clear of the cord!","Flamer warming up! Back off!","Cover me, I'm reloading!","Target's in the trees! Shoot!","Drop him before he reaches the stairs!","Ambush the ridge! Hold!","Vulture circling! Stay sharp!","On my signal, we take him alive!"],"jhunter":["Your fear is loud, Sith. I hear it from here.","The Order sent its best. You are merely the last.","I sense the echo of your master in your blade.","Turn from the dark. Then the Force may spare you.","You have killed many. The Force remembers each one.","Your hatred has a scent. I follow it.","Hold, Sith. There is still a choice to make.","Do you feel the light? It is no longer afraid of you.","I see the cracks in your center. Ready yourself.","Kneel, or stand and be undone.","You rage like a child. Calm yourself.","The Jedi were broken once. We remember that.","I will not spill your blood needlessly.","Your power is a wound. Let me close it.","The darkness has a sound. Yours is screaming.","We are not the Order that fell. We rebuild.","Your shadow walks ahead of you. It is weak.","Stop running. The Force tires of your pattern.","Feel the center. Let it pull you back to me.","I have seen the last of your kind. You are next.","The Force wavers. I falter.","My center is gone! Find it for me!","Your blade is cold, Sith.","Shield failing. Hold my line!","The light dims... only for a breath.","Good strike, Sith. Good strike.","Pain is a teacher. I will listen.","Focus broken. Cover me!","The echoes call me. Let me rest.","I can still sense you. Still sensing.","My hand. I cannot hold the hilt.","The Force hurts. It always hurts near you.","Hold the line for the Order!","I will return, Sith. I always do.","You do not win. You merely continue.","Breathe. The forest breathes with you.","The seeker says the pulse is here. Look closer.","A pulse echoes under the stone. Listen.","Still water, still mind. We wait.","Do not rush the pattern. Watch the leaves.","A Sith's footstep leaves a mark in the Force.","Find the center. Then find him.","The echoes thicken here. Be careful.","Hush. Listen to what the jungle says.","Your fear reveals your path, Sith.","We were a light once. We will be again.","Stay calm. Calm is the true weapon.","Dark echoes at the tomb. Mark the spot.","I sense the mask, and the mask senses me.","Patience. The Force hides nothing from us.","Seeker to all: the pulse is north!","Flank! Use the Force to shield the line!","Pull him from the altar! Now!","Push him off the ledge! Strike!","Focus on the center! Do not waver!","Sith using the terrain! Adjust!","Break his rhythm! Feint left!","Converge on the echo! Hold!","Cut off his retreat! Block the path!","Saber lock! Hold him where he stands!"],"assassin":["Your Order is already a corpse. We dig the graves.","The Shroud sees you. It has watched for days.","Come closer. The dark is kind to the patient.","The temple is ours now. Go kneel in it.","Feel the cold? That is our blade's breath.","Milian's apprentice will wipe that smile away.","Let your light hunt you. Let it come.","Every step you take, a knife is listening.","We're shadows. You were watching the wrong tree.","Pick a hilt, Jedi. We'll bury it.","The Harbinger's name is ours. So is your grave.","Your prayers taste bitter. Keep them.","We don't kill fast. We kill finally.","One breath, one cut. That is the whole lesson.","The dark does not ask permission, Jedi.","You left your back open. We noticed.","The rumor you chase stands behind you.","You fight like the Order: loud and late.","Our master does not forgive. Neither do we.","Pick your last breath carefully, Jedi.","Hold the line! Don't let him through!","Hurt, not down. Still striking.","Blade's cracked. Switching to the pike!","Vaara, cover my left side!","Shield's cooked. Eren, take it!","Cut my arm, I still bite.","I'll bleed for the Shroud. It's worth it.","Next round, we finish this together.","Stealth down! Get behind the pillar!","Pain is a lesson. I've learned it before.","Don't drag me. Keep fighting!","I'm fine. Keep the lane open.","Falling back to the altar! Cover me!","My mask's cracked. My face is cold.","I will not fall in the open. Not here.","Silence is the weapon. Keep it.","Count the exits. Count them again.","Whisper to the stone. It listens back.","The stealth field flickers. Check the generator.","Rain brings the scent. Track him by it.","The Lord's holocron is watching. Do not fail.","Don't stare at the sky. The sky is empty.","Keep your pike level. Keep your breath slow.","Patience. Prey always walks back to its den.","The ward hums. Dangerous. Stand back.","The base smells of smoke. Good.","I can still hear the Padawan's voice. Ignore it.","Stop sleeping in the niche, Irrin. It's rude.","Our names are carved in the stone. Remember them.","Breathe through the mask. In. Out. Hold.","Flank the north stair! Move!","Stealth field up! Drop back!","Pike in! Strike the throat!","Dagger out! Sleeve clear!","Overwatch on the canopy! Eyes up!","Lure him to the trap! Keep moving!","Converge on Lord Rathatri! Shield him!","Cut the rope! Drop the Jedi!","Hold the ward! Keep the sparks away!","Clear the crypt! Clear it now!"],"trandoshan":["Hunt begins. Scorekeeper watches close.","You small. Small things run. Run now.","Meat with legs. Good hunt.","Mine. Tally it, Keeper. Mine.","Show teeth, prey. Show them.","Your Jedi cloth pretty. Will tear nice.","Trophy for my rack. Just a small one.","Bosskarr sends greeting. Hard greeting.","Count this one! Keeper, count!","You run. We hunt. Old game.","Skullrender, come! Kill the runner!","Blood smells sweet. Scorekeeper smiles.","I hunt for the Hutts and for my honor.","No trade. No deal. Only prey.","Your tomb is our tally. Hear it.","Stalker's Shadow! Strike from above!","Trandoshan hunt is patient. You are not.","Mine, mine! Quick, before the Keeper sees.","Look at the scales. We are older than your fear.","Hiss at the dark. Dark hisses back.","Ssk! Scale torn!","Scorekeeper, forgive this wound.","That hurt. Good hurt. Mark it.","Blood on scales. Scorekeeper sees.","Bah! Shot in the leg! Keep moving.","Gunner down! Take his rifle!","My arm burns. Keep shooting!","I pay debt in blood. Pay it now.","Not today, Sith. Not this hunt.","Scale cracked. Hurts. Still hunting.","Medic! Scorekeeper, help!","You strike well. I remember.","Fine. Mine is short. Yours is shorter.","Hurts! Next, you bleed more!","I fall, but the Keeper tallies me standing.","Wait. Prey always returns to water.","Sun on the mud. Warm. Good hunting.","Bosskarr counts cargo. We count prey.","Hunt is quiet. Hunt is patient.","My rifle hungers. Feed it.","Smell that? Forest blood, ours and theirs.","Old tale: the Scorekeeper keeps a long book.","Rest now. Hunt tonight.","Watch the reeds. Something moves.","Sith-thing pays well. Keep your rifle warm.","Clean the claws. Clean them twice.","Ship's nose dips. Heavy load today.","Eat the ration, then hunt.","Water's cold. Tallies are warm.","Patience is the first skill.","Flank them! Circle wide, quiet!","Net up! Hold him in the net!","Rifle ready! Pick the target!","Climb the ridge! Shoot down!","Move, move! Go, go!","Herd them to the mud!","Drag the wounded! Take the runner!","Skullrender, blast the wall!","Wait for my signal! Then strike!","Hold the crossing! No retreat!"],"exchange":["The Exchange collects. Always.","Nobody walks off the Promenade with Exchange goods.","Cut him off at the lift!","Boss wants the amulet, not the body. Mostly.","He's a Force-user. Shoot first, invoice later.","Every debt gets paid on this moon.","Flank him by the kiosks!","Credits or blood, Jedi-thing. Pick one."]},"scenes":{"1_1_cold_open":{"id":"1_1_cold_open","act":1,"loc":"Hutta: black frame over the arena roar","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"3951 BBY. The Sith Triumvirate is ash.","dur":3.7,"cam":"black frame"},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Jedi are few.","dur":2.5},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"In the cracks between, something hungry is growing.","dur":4.1},{"who":"CROWD","line":"Four-Two-Six! Blood! Four-Two-Six!","dur":2.2,"cam":"arena roar; hard cut"},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"They called me a number. I answered it until I hated it.","dur":5.6,"cam":"close on scarred hands"}],"choice":null},"1_2_the_pit":{"id":"1_2_the_pit","act":1,"loc":"Hutta: cantina-yard pit, shiv tutorial","shots":[{"who":"VAK","line":"Bets are open! Four-Two-Six fights for the Hutt's pleasure!","dur":4.5,"cam":"wide, ringside"},{"who":"CROWD","line":"Scars for the coin! Scars for the coin!","dur":4.1},{"who":"SYS","line":"Shiv: LMB strike. Shift to dodge. Survive the bell.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Three of them and one shiv. Better odds than usual.","dur":4.8,"cam":"over shoulder"},{"who":"VAK","line":"Don't let him breathe! Feed the crowd!","dur":3.7}],"choice":null},"1_3_losing_fight":{"id":"1_3_losing_fight","act":1,"loc":"Hutta: pit, losing fight, first Force surge","shots":[{"who":"VAK","line":"Three to one, and the odds are melting! Down he goes!","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Not yet. Get off me.","dur":2.9,"cam":"dutch angle, slow"},{"who":"SYS","line":"Pain threshold low. Survival instinct engaged.","dur":3.3},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I'm not done. Not here, not like this.","dur":4.1},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Something answers the rage.","dur":2.5,"cam":"whiteout; rage FX"},{"who":"CROWD","line":"Look at him! The air's bending!","dur":3.3},{"who":"VAK","line":"What in the Hutt's name was that?","dur":3.7},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"There you are.","dur":2.2,"cam":"gallery, hooded silhouette"}],"choice":null},"1_4_milians_test":{"id":"1_4_milians_test","act":1,"loc":"Hutta: second staged fight, Force-push tutorial","shots":[{"who":"VAK","line":"A lady from off-world paid for this one. Live, or don't.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Who's paying? Tell me who wants me dead.","dur":4.1},{"who":"VAK","line":"Someone with a voice like a grave and a fat purse. Fight!","dur":5.6},{"who":"SYS","line":"Push: F. Shove the blade-men off the ledge.","dur":4.1},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Fine. Then I'll be the one left standing.","dur":4.1},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Survive the second bell.","dur":2.5}],"choice":null},"1_5_the_offer":{"id":"1_5_the_offer","act":1,"loc":"Hutta: disused storage chamber beneath the holdings","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Four-Two-Six is taken without a name.","dur":3.3,"cam":"POV, hooded guards walking"},{"who":"GUARD","line":"Move. Don't look at her.","dur":2.9},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Leave us.","dur":1.8,"cam":"close, steel-grey hair, piercing eyes"},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"You are persistent. Like a parasite that refuses to die. That caught my interest.","dur":6.4},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Everyone wants something from a pit slave. Say it.","dur":4.5},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"What you did in the arena... it wasn't skill or training.","dur":5.2},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"There's a hunger in you, something… raw.","dur":3.7},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"The Force flows through all life, but most are oblivious to it.","dur":5.6},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"You clawed at it instinctively.","dur":2.9},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Force. That's a word priests and liars use.","dur":4.1},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"I offer you a choice. Remain here, a beast for the crowd's amusement until you die in agony.","dur":7.9},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Or come with me, learn what power you possess, and forge a different kind of existence.","dur":7.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"What makes you different from my other masters?","dur":4.1},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Nothing. I make no promises of freedom. Only a different leash.","dur":5.2}],"choice":{"prompt":"Answer the witch.","A":{"text":"I'll come. Teach me the hunger.","consequence":"Cosmetic. Same road; Milian names him Rathatri.","next":"1_6_years_in_minutes","set":null},"B":{"text":"Then kill me here, witch.","consequence":"Cosmetic. Same road; Milian only says: Not yet.","next":"1_6_years_in_minutes","set":null}}},"1_6_years_in_minutes":{"id":"1_6_years_in_minutes","act":1,"loc":"Hutta to Zx34: departure, then training montage","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Hutta's lights fall away under cover of darkness.","dur":4.1,"cam":"shuttle, cloud layer"},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Good. Leave the number here. Bring only your hunger.","dur":4.5},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"YEARS PASS.","dur":1.8,"cam":"timelapse, hands assemble a hilt"},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Pain is a door, Rathatri. Walk through it, or stay on the hinges.","dur":6.0},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I'm through. Again.","dur":2.2},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Again. Build the hilt with your hands, not your fear.","dur":4.8},{"who":"SYS","line":"Bone-hilt assembly: 14 hours. Do not drop the crystal.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"It's... it's alive.","dur":2.2,"cam":"first crimson ignition"},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"It's hungry. Like you. Feed it with discipline.","dur":4.1},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Study the scrolls. Dead Sith have more to teach than living Jedi.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Teach me what they built, not only what they lost.","dur":4.8},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Ruins are for the sentimental. Keep your eyes on the dagger.","dur":5.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Years of study. Years of pain. The hunger never sleeps.","dur":4.8}],"choice":null},"1_7_milian_dies":{"id":"1_7_milian_dies","act":1,"loc":"Zx34 sanctum: Milian's last stand (scripted loss)","shots":[{"who":"KYROS","line":"Milian. Your war ends in this sanctum.","dur":3.7,"cam":"Kyros in doorway, dual blue blades"},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Aiden Kyros. You have aged like a grudge.","dur":4.1},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Your kind does not age, Milian. It only decays.","dur":4.5},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Master, the wards are down. Two more behind us.","dur":4.5},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Ah. The little Padawan. Did she bring a sword or a sermon?","dur":5.6},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Both. Hold still, witch.","dur":2.5},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Rathatri. Take the grimoire. Run.","dur":2.9},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Not without you!","dur":2.2,"cam":"close, crimson blade ignites"},{"who":"SYS","line":"Scripted loss. You cannot win this. Learn the dodge.","dur":4.5},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Do not mourn me. Mourning is for those who still have something to lose.","dur":6.4},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Sith die the way they lived. Alone.","dur":3.7},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Master, he's running!","dur":2.2},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Let him. A rumor is harder to kill than a man.","dur":5.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"DARK LEGACY","dur":1.8,"cam":"title card, red lightning crack"}],"choice":null},"2_1_junker_crash":{"id":"2_1_junker_crash","act":2,"loc":"Dxun: The Harbinger slams into a jungle clearing","shots":[{"who":"SYS","line":"HYPERDRIVE: STALLED. LIFE SUPPORT: FLICKERING. HULL: 61 PERCENT.","dur":4.1},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Hold together, you rust-eaten coffin. Hold.","dur":3.3},{"who":"COMM","line":"(static) Unknown freighter, identify yourself.","dur":2.9},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Nobody comes to this moon. That's the only reason I came.","dur":5.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Dxun. The demon moon of Onderon. Its jungle keeps what it is given.","dur":6.0},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"A moon of beasts and dead Sith. I've lived in worse pens.","dur":5.6}],"choice":null},"2_2_bosskarr_ambush":{"id":"2_2_bosskarr_ambush","act":2,"loc":"Dxun: causeway ambush on a Trandoshan slaver party","shots":[{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Scorekeeper watches. Who walks into my hunt-road?","dur":3.7},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Your road ends here, lizard. Open the cargo hold.","dur":4.5},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Pit-thing. Vak's favorite. I remember your stink.","dur":3.7},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then you remember I'm still alive. Your cargo can't say the same.","dur":5.6},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Cargo counts little. Scorekeeper counts every breath.","dur":3.7},{"who":"SYS","line":"Guards down. Bosskarr's rifle lies in the mud.","dur":4.1},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Kill me, or hear the Scorekeeper's terms.","dur":3.7,"cam":"Bosskarr on his knees, scarred snout"}],"choice":{"prompt":"The Trandoshan kneels. Spare him, or end his tally?","A":{"text":"Speak your terms.","consequence":"Life-debt sworn. Bosskarr serves; slaver intel and merchandise unlocked.","next":"2_2a_life_debt_oath","set":null},"B":{"text":"End your tally, lizard.","consequence":"Bosskarr dies. His ships break orbit. Merchandise lost. HEAT +5.","next":"2_2b_tally_broken","set":null}}},"2_2a_life_debt_oath":{"id":"2_2a_life_debt_oath","act":2,"loc":"Dxun causeway: the life-debt oath","branch_of":"2_2_bosskarr_ambush","shots":[{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Life spared. Life owed. The Scorekeeper writes it in the ledger.","dur":5.2},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Your breath now sits in my blood. I carry your hunt.","dur":5.2},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Bosskarr, tally-keeper of Jagganath's Fang. Skullrender and Stalker's Shadow answer my tally.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Terms. Merchandise first. Force-sensitives, not scrap.","dur":3.3},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Force-things. Two in my hold now. More after the next hunt.","dur":5.2},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Trandoshan ledger never lies. The Scorekeeper forgets nothing, not even your face.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then keep your mouth shut about my face.","dur":4.1},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Silence is also a mark. The Scorekeeper counts it.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then count this. Break the oath and I take your ledger and your tail.","dur":6.4},{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"Oath is mine. Life-debt, until I die or you do.","dur":4.8,"cam":"Bosskarr lowers his head"}],"choice":null},"2_2b_tally_broken":{"id":"2_2b_tally_broken","act":2,"loc":"Dxun causeway: the tally ends","branch_of":"2_2_bosskarr_ambush","shots":[{"who":"BOSSKARR","line":"The Scorekeeper marks you, Sith-thing. Marks you for the next hunt.","dur":5.2},{"who":"SYS","line":"Bosskarr's last breath. Skullrender and Stalker's Shadow break orbit.","dur":4.5},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The slave runs on Dxun go quiet. A blood-feud begins.","dur":4.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Let them come. I'll tally every one of them.","dur":4.5}],"choice":null},"2_3_starving_beast":{"id":"2_3_starving_beast","act":2,"loc":"Dxun deep jungle: the recruits' trial","shots":[{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Five recruits. One ration pack each, and a temple at the end of the trail.","dur":6.8},{"who":"RECRUIT","line":"Please. We'll follow you. We'll follow.","dur":3.3},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"You'll follow. I know. That's the problem with followers.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RECRUIT","line":"Her leg is broken. She can't keep up with us.","dur":4.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then the jungle decides. Not me. Not you.","dur":4.1},{"who":"SYS","line":"Predator scent: maalraas pack, 300 m. Weak prey draws them.","dur":4.8,"cam":"wide, canopy"}],"choice":{"prompt":"The wounded will not reach the temple. Decide.","A":{"text":"Leave them to the jungle.","consequence":"Survivors' loyalty +5. The wounded are lost. HEAT 0.","next":"2_4_first_artifact","set":null},"B":{"text":"Cull the wounded before the predators do.","consequence":"Survivors' fear +10. Loyalty bought with terror.","next":"2_4_first_artifact","set":null}}},"2_4_first_artifact":{"id":"2_4_first_artifact","act":2,"loc":"Dxun: tomb fringe, roots over a buried holocron","shots":[{"who":"SYS","line":"ECHO DETECTED. Hold Tab to pulse the roots.","dur":4.1},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Under the tomb roots, something whispers.","dur":3.3,"cam":"dig site, pulse ring"},{"who":"HOLOCRON","line":"Not... the hand. It was never Milian's hand.","dur":4.1},{"who":"HOLOCRON","line":"She kept the names from you. Ask her what she hid.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Who are you? Show yourself.","dur":2.9},{"who":"HOLOCRON","line":"The one before you. Breathe, and I will be quiet.","dur":4.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then talk while I breathe. Who was first?","dur":4.1},{"who":"HOLOCRON","line":"First burned, last forgotten. Like all her students.","dur":4.1},{"who":"SYS","line":"Corrupted Holocron secured. Visions unlocked. Force regen +10 percent.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I'll find the rest of your lesson, and decide if it's true.","dur":5.6}],"choice":null},"2_5_traya_judgment":{"id":"2_5_traya_judgment","act":2,"loc":"Dxun temple: command table, Traya's holocron wakes","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The holocron wakes. A hooded figure turns toward him.","dur":4.5,"cam":"orbit around holocron"},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Is the death of the Jedi enough?","dur":3.7},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"What will you do once they are gone?","dur":4.1},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"What form will your power take?","dur":3.3},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I haven't decided. I suppose you'll tell me.","dur":4.1},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Your connection to the Force is undeniable. It seethes with hatred, pulses with desperation.","dur":6.4},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Yet, it is akin to a caged beast, unleashed with force but little direction.","dur":6.4},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then give it direction. Teach me.","dur":3.3},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Teaching is not what I do. I sharpen. There is a difference, and you will learn it in blood.","dur":8.3},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Do you understand the difference between using the dark side, and being consumed by it?","dur":6.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I was eaten by a pit for years. Ask the pit.","dur":5.2},{"who":"SYS","line":"Upgrade tree unlocked: THE CAGE.","dur":2.9}],"choice":null},"2_6_first_hunters":{"id":"2_6_first_hunters","act":2,"loc":"Dxun north ridge: a bounty hunter pair drops in","shots":[{"who":"COMM","line":"Two hunter drops on the north ridge. Jet packs warm.","dur":4.8},{"who":"ROE","line":"Bounty's on a rumor. Pays well. Dead or breathing, same fee.","dur":5.2},{"who":"ROE","line":"Smells like a Sith, sounds like a cave. Let's go, partner.","dur":5.2},{"who":"HUNTER","line":"Ghost in the canopy. Check your left.","dur":3.7}],"choice":{"prompt":"Two hunters hover over the clearing. Who hunts whom?","A":{"text":"Ambush from the canopy.","consequence":"Both hunters down. HEAT +2. Trophy: first hilt on the wall.","next":"3_1_ambria","set":null},"B":{"text":"Let the boma pack take them.","consequence":"Hunters vanish into the ferns. Trophy: first hilt on the wall. HEAT 0.","next":"3_1_ambria","set":null}}},"3_1_ambria":{"id":"3_1_ambria","act":3,"loc":"Ambria: obsidian lakes and the echo of a rival-lord duel","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Ambria. Obsidian lakes. Two rival lords, one dead ground.","dur":4.5,"cam":"wide over glassy lake"},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"You fixate on the echoes of these so-called legends, not the reality of their rise.","dur":6.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Do you think they were born masters?","dur":3.7},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"They crawled through filth, betrayed and were betrayed, lost more than they ever gained.","dur":6.4},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Do you see their empires now? Dust and echoes.","dur":4.5},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Are you willing to sacrifice everything and leave behind the same?","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Two lords, one knife. Look at the ground where the second bell rang.","dur":6.0},{"who":"SYS","line":"Echo: rival lords duel. Betrayal at the second bell.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"It's crying. The crystal is crying.","dur":3.3},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Then listen to it. Do not let it sing for you.","dur":5.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Tainted Kyber secured. Rage surge unlocked (V). Each use ticks corruption.","dur":5.2}],"choice":null},"3_2_the_seizure":{"id":"3_2_the_seizure","act":3,"loc":"Outer Rim wreck field: Force domination of a Sith Interceptor","shots":[{"who":"COMM","line":"Umbral Wake, port thruster is walking! Somebody answer me!","dur":4.5},{"who":"DONN","line":"Lieutenant Donn, Umbral Wake. Mayday! Stabilizers aren't holding!","dur":4.1},{"who":"SYS","line":"DOMINATE channel: hold T for 2.5 seconds. Any hit cancels.","dur":4.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Do not seize the hull. Seize the will that holds it. Find the cracks.","dur":6.4},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Port engine. There. The weak flaw. Feed it.","dur":4.1},{"who":"DONN","line":"It's pulling me! I have the stick, I have the... no. No!","dur":5.6},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Feed on the terror, not the wound. Their panic is your current.","dur":5.6},{"who":"DONN","line":"I was promoted two weeks ago. Please, I'm twenty-one...","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then you'll be the youngest name on my wall. Hold still.","dur":5.2},{"who":"SYS","line":"Engine breach. Tractor beam engaged. Interceptor secured.","dur":3.7},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Umbral Wake drops out of the sky and into the Harbinger's grip.","dur":6.0},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Nightbringer. Burn the old name off the hull.","dur":4.1,"cam":"Harbinger bridge, crimson glow"}],"choice":{"prompt":"The lieutenant is still breathing in the wreck. Decide.","A":{"text":"Drag the lieutenant out alive.","consequence":"Interrogation intel on Jedi patrols. HEAT -2.","next":"3_3_raxus","set":null},"B":{"text":"Leave him in the drifting hulk.","consequence":"The rumor spreads: fear +10. HEAT +4.","next":"3_3_raxus","set":null}}},"3_3_raxus":{"id":"3_3_raxus","act":3,"loc":"Raxus Prime: Confederacy ruins under an ash-grey sky","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Raxus Prime. Confederacy ruins under an ash-grey sky.","dur":4.1,"cam":"ruin, rain of ash"},{"who":"DB","line":"Statement: Jedi forms are predictable, Master. Predictable is fatal.","dur":4.5},{"who":"DB","line":"Query: Shall I catalogue the Raxus dead, or the Raxus forms?","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"The forms. The dead can wait in your memory banks.","dur":4.8},{"who":"DB","line":"Affirmative. Analysis: parry windows telegraph. Breathing before a strike is a confession.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then show me their confession.","dur":2.9},{"who":"DB","line":"Statement: Pattern-breaking is cheaper than strength. Strike the rhythm, not the wrist.","dur":5.6},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Thousands died here. Their despair ripples. Learn to ride the ripple.","dur":5.2},{"who":"SYS","line":"PATTERN-BREAKER acquired. Jedi parry windows now telegraphed to you.","dur":4.5}],"choice":null},"3_4_celene_duel_1":{"id":"3_4_celene_duel_1","act":3,"loc":"Raxus Prime: foundry hall, Celene Tryst's first duel (boss)","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Raxus foundry hall. Celene Tryst has tracked the rumor.","dur":4.5,"cam":"wide, conveyor lines"},{"who":"CELENE","line":"You're the one who ran from Milian's sanctum. Hiding, or waiting?","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I don't hide. Ask the dead witch.","dur":3.7},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Kyros said you'd run. I said you'd crawl first.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then you'll learn what crawling costs.","dur":3.3},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Show me what you learned from Milian's blood.","dur":4.1},{"who":"CELENE","line":"You fight like a stray with a stolen blade. Predictable.","dur":4.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Predictable ends at a trap. Your footing, Padawan. Not mine.","dur":4.8},{"who":"SYS","line":"Conveyor collapse. Celene staggers, then rises, bleeding.","dur":3.7},{"who":"CELENE","line":"You cheated.","dur":1.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I survived. The rest is just words.","dur":3.7},{"who":"CELENE","line":"There's no honor in a trap.","dur":3.3},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"There's no honor in a corpse, Padawan. Ask Milian's.","dur":4.5},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Next time, I won't give you the ground.","dur":4.1},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Your victories hinge on your victims' mistakes, not your mastery.","dur":4.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"You exploit terrain, manipulate the weak-minded.","dur":3.3},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Face a truly disciplined foe, and your skill crumbles like the ruins you cling to.","dur":6.8},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Training arc unlocked. Celene Tryst survives.","dur":3.3}],"choice":null},"3_5_rebuild":{"id":"3_5_rebuild","act":3,"loc":"Dxun temple: study hall and assassin dispatch board","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Dxun temple. The study hall smells of ozone and old incense.","dur":5.2,"cam":"log board"},{"who":"EREN","line":"Milian leaned left twice. A man who leans gets knocked over.","dur":5.2},{"who":"VAARA","line":"Kyros never overextends. Except once. Look at this frame.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Milian let him see the pattern. Then she taught him the lesson wrong.","dur":6.0},{"who":"EREN","line":"Then nobody sees ours. Burned fields grow back, if you hide the fire.","dur":6.0},{"who":"VAARA","line":"Give me a target. I'd rather bleed for you than sit in this temple.","dur":6.4},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Dispatch board open. Available: Vaara, Eren, and the Elite Five.","dur":4.8},{"who":"SYS","line":"Pattern analysis: match three openings to unlock the Kyros lesson.","dur":4.8}],"choice":null},"4_1_krayiss":{"id":"4_1_krayiss","act":4,"loc":"Krayiss II: dead forest, a warm ritual circle","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Krayiss II. A dead forest of bone-white bark. One ritual circle, still warm.","dur":6.0,"cam":"ritual ground"},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Focus is a blade. Dull it with fear, and it will not cut your own hand.","dur":7.2},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Isolation is strength only until it becomes your cage.","dur":4.5},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"The binding. What is the price for a zakkeg guardian?","dur":4.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"A night of your sleep. And a fragment of your certainty.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Hold still, beast. You're mine now. Breathe with me.","dur":4.5},{"who":"SYS","line":"Ritual of Binding: stage 2 of 3. Hold the sigil steady.","dur":5.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Zakkeg guardian bound. Base defense events unlocked.","dur":3.7}],"choice":null},"4_2_lenico":{"id":"4_2_lenico","act":4,"loc":"Lenico IV: reality folds, sensory illusions","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Lenico IV. Reality folds like wet cloth. Energy readings scream.","dur":4.8,"cam":"aurora, distortion"},{"who":"MILIAN","line":"Rathatri. The parasite, still crawling after me?","dur":3.7},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"You're not her. She's ash on Zx34.","dur":3.7},{"who":"MIRROR","line":"Then what are you, Rathatri? A pit slave with a borrowed blade.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Mirror. Shatter.","dur":1.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Do not fear the mirror, Rathatri. Wonder what it sees.","dur":4.8},{"who":"MIRROR","line":"You still flinch when the whip cracks. I was always watching.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then watch this.","dur":2.2,"cam":"strike through the mirror"},{"who":"SYS","line":"Illusions dispelled. Mask of Despair acquired: Jedi seekers lose lock.","dur":4.8}],"choice":null},"4_3_the_shroud":{"id":"4_3_the_shroud","act":4,"loc":"Dxun landing ring: seven assassins and the Shroud descends","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Dxun landing ring. Seven assassins stand in a circle. Above, a shape comes down through the canopy.","dur":7.5,"cam":"wide, the Shroud descends"},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Seven knives. One Shroud. Which of you do I trust?","dur":4.8},{"who":"VAARA","line":"Trust the one who bleeds for you.","dur":3.7},{"who":"EREN","line":"Trust the one who never needs to be asked twice.","dur":4.8},{"who":"IRRIN","line":"We kneel to the Shroud. We kneel to you once you've earned it.","dur":6.0},{"who":"SSARRA","line":"The ledger says you owe us rest. Pay it, or we keep counting.","dur":6.0},{"who":"DORN","line":"Name the target. I'll count the dead, same as always.","dur":4.8},{"who":"PELL","line":"I drew the enclave's map myself. I can walk it blind.","dur":5.2},{"who":"MESK","line":"I've never seen a Jedi. I hope they're slower than the holovids.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then earn yourselves a place in my shadow. Every one of you.","dur":5.6},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Shroud descends. Vantablack hull. Stealth runs add no HEAT.","dur":4.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"A shroud is a kindness only to the one who hides beneath it.","dur":6.0}],"choice":null},"4_4_iziz_strike":{"id":"4_4_iziz_strike","act":4,"loc":"Onderon: Iziz streets, the tomb key-fragment vault","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Onderon. Iziz streets. The tomb key lies in the city's oldest vault.","dur":5.6,"cam":"city verticality"},{"who":"KEEL","line":"Contact! Sith on the north bridge. Shields up!","dur":4.1},{"who":"KEEL","line":"Target is a Sith. Repeat, Sith. Form the shield wall.","dur":4.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Your line is shorter than your hope, Sergeant.","dur":4.1},{"who":"KEEL","line":"Hope's got armor, Sith. Your mouth doesn't.","dur":3.7},{"who":"KEEL","line":"Shield wall! Shields up, form on me!","dur":3.7},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"You're the wall, Sergeant. I'm the crack in it.","dur":4.5},{"who":"KEEL","line":"Shield's down! Medic, shield's down! Hold the line!","dur":4.1},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Lay down the shield and live.","dur":3.3},{"who":"KEEL","line":"Tell the Republic... the Sith came through the wall.","dur":4.5},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Tomb key-fragment recovered. Militia pursuit raises HEAT.","dur":3.7}],"choice":null},"4_5_nadds_tomb":{"id":"4_5_nadds_tomb","act":4,"loc":"Dxun: the iron mausoleum and Freedon Nadd's spirit","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Dxun. The iron mausoleum. Spiked bastion, obsidian steps.","dur":4.1,"cam":"iron gates"},{"who":"NADD","line":"Who disturbs the iron? Who stirs the dead?","dur":4.1},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"A student, my lord. Looking for a teacher.","dur":4.1},{"who":"NADD","line":"I was a lord once. Your kind crawls through my halls and calls it wisdom.","dur":6.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Then show me the way down, Lord Nadd. Teach me wisdom.","dur":5.2},{"who":"NADD","line":"Prove the hunger, and the shard is yours. Walk the orbalisk stairs.","dur":5.6},{"who":"SYS","line":"Orbalisk spores in the air. Keep moving.","dur":3.7},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Freedon Nadd's holocron shard acquired.","dur":2.9},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Dxun. The Nadd tomb has woken. I felt it in my bones.","dur":5.6},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Gather the cell. We go to the demon moon.","dur":4.5},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Master, is the Sith ours to end?","dur":3.7},{"who":"KYROS","line":"All Sith are ours to end, Padawan. This one first.","dur":4.8}],"choice":null},"5_1_base_siege":{"id":"5_1_base_siege","act":5,"loc":"Dxun temple: the Kyros hunt cell assaults the base","shots":[{"who":"KYROS","line":"Surrender the temple, Sith. Or we burn the jungle around it.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"You'll have to find the temple first, Battlemaster.","dur":4.1},{"who":"SYS","line":"WARD STONE: hold the sequence. Three keys, one chance each.","dur":4.8},{"who":"IRRIN","line":"We hold, Lord! For the Shroud!","dur":3.3,"cond":"loyalty:high"},{"who":"IRRIN","line":"Find your own grave, Rathatri. I'm not your shield anymore.","dur":4.8,"cond":"loyalty:low"},{"who":"VAARA","line":"I hold the east stair. Go to the altar and finish the ward.","dur":6.0,"cond":"loyalty:high"},{"who":"VAARA","line":"My blades are cold. Hold your own ward, Lord.","dur":4.5,"cond":"loyalty:low"},{"who":"EREN","line":"I stand because I'm not finished with the Jedi yet.","dur":4.8,"cond":"loyalty:high"},{"who":"EREN","line":"Fear is the only thing keeping my feet here. Fear is a poor master.","dur":6.4,"cond":"loyalty:low"},{"who":"SYS","line":"Ward malfunction. Sparks. The stone flickers.","dur":3.3},{"who":"SYS","line":"Zakkeg guardian unleashed.","dur":2.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"HEAT 100. The hunt cell is inside the walls.","dur":4.5}],"choice":null},"5_2_kyros_boss":{"id":"5_2_kyros_boss","act":5,"loc":"Dxun temple, Nadd crypt: Aiden Kyros, three phases","shots":[{"who":"KYROS","line":"I have buried better Sith than you, Rathatri. Each one swore he was different.","dur":6.4,"phase":1},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Your rage is loud. Your footwork is louder.","dur":4.1,"phase":1},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I don't need quiet. I need you dead.","dur":4.1,"phase":1},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Breathe, Sith. Your rage is a window, and I can see through it.","dur":6.0,"phase":2},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Battle meditation. Hold. Let your anger show me its shape.","dur":4.8,"phase":2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Shape? You'll see the shape of my blade.","dur":4.1,"phase":2},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Let go of it. The blade is not yours. It never was.","dur":5.6,"phase":3},{"who":"KYROS","line":"Disarm. Breathe. Stand down, and die a Jedi's enemy, not a Sith's tool.","dur":6.0,"phase":3},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"I die a Sith. You'll be the reason.","dur":4.1,"phase":3},{"who":"SYS","line":"DISARM: time the blade-lock. Break the grip on his hilts.","dur":4.8},{"who":"KYROS","line":"You fought like a rumor, Sith. Let the Order remember your name.","dur":5.6}],"choice":null},"5_3_celene_choice":{"id":"5_3_celene_choice","act":5,"loc":"Dxun ruined altar: Celene arrives on foot, her saber dark","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The ruined altar. Celene arrives on foot, her saber dark.","dur":4.8,"cam":"Celene in grey knight robes"},{"who":"CELENE","line":"The enclave's gone. The Wellspring took them. They turned on each other.","dur":5.6},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Halun Tesk couldn't stop seeing his own fear. I couldn't reach him.","dur":5.6},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"You came alone. That's the first wise thing your Order taught you.","dur":5.6},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Kyros is dead. You did that. You did all of it.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Yes. Now say what you want. Say it.","dur":4.1},{"who":"CELENE","line":"I want nothing you can give me, Sith.","dur":4.1}],"choice":{"prompt":"The Padawan is at your feet. What is her end?","A":{"text":"Execute her. Add her hilt to the wall.","consequence":"Trophy gained. Celene dies. Path: Execute.","next":"5_4_darth_question","set":{"celene":"execute"}},"B":{"text":"Corrupt her. Make her kneel to the Shroud.","consequence":"Celene kneels, broken and loyal. Path: Corrupt.","next":"5_4_darth_question","set":{"celene":"corrupt"}}}},"5_4_darth_question":{"id":"5_4_darth_question","act":5,"loc":"Dxun command table: Traya's final judgment","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Celene's end, as chosen.","dur":2.5,"cam":"altar, Celene's fate"},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Tell Kyros... I did not kneel.","dur":3.3,"cond":"celene:execute"},{"who":"CELENE","line":"Yes, Lord Rathatri. Whatever you command.","dur":3.3,"cond":"celene:corrupt"},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Look at your circle, Rathatri. Seven knives, each one waiting for your mistake.","dur":6.0},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"The title 'Darth' is earned by crushing those who came before, not by saying it.","dur":6.8},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Are you ready to murder your own assassins for this hollow title?","dur":5.6},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Perhaps taking the title will inflame your ambition further.","dur":4.5},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Or accelerate your own self-destruction. A fascinating experiment.","dur":4.1}],"choice":{"prompt":"Claim the title over their kneeling loyalty, or purge them for their fear?","A":{"text":"Claim the title. Keep the kneeling blades.","consequence":"The assassins kneel and you accept the name.","next":{"execute":"end_a_reaper","corrupt":"end_true_darth"},"set":null},"B":{"text":"Purge the roster. Fear is loyalty enough.","consequence":"The roster falls. You stand alone with the title.","next":{"execute":"end_dark_warrens","corrupt":"end_b_corrupter"},"set":null}}},"end_a_reaper":{"id":"end_a_reaper","act":5,"loc":"Ending A: Execute + Claim","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Shroud rises over Dxun. The Jedi have a new name for their fear.","dur":6.4},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"You killed the Order's last symbol and kept the cult. The rebuild learns to fear your ships.","dur":7.5},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"THE REAPER OF THE REBUILD.","dur":2.9}],"choice":null},"end_b_corrupter":{"id":"end_b_corrupter","act":5,"loc":"Ending B: Corrupt + Purge","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Celene kneels in the ash of the enclave, her light a candle you relit as your own.","dur":7.5},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Your assassins are dust. Her faith is the only blade you have left, and she keeps it sharp.","dur":7.9},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"THE CORRUPTER.","dur":1.8}],"choice":null},"end_true_darth":{"id":"end_true_darth","act":5,"loc":"Ending True: Corrupt + Claim","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Dxun canopy closes over the temple. The kneeling blades rise as one.","dur":6.0},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Traya's holocron dims: a fascinating experiment. The title is yours, for now.","dur":5.6},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"DARTH RATHATRI.","dur":1.8}],"choice":null},"end_dark_warrens":{"id":"end_dark_warrens","act":5,"loc":"Ending Dark: Execute + Purge","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The assassins' niches stand empty. The Shroud launches with no crew to answer its bell.","dur":6.8},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"Only the zakkeg keeps watch at the threshold. No one is left to tell your story.","dur":7.2},{"who":"CAPTION","line":"ALONE IN THE WARRENS.","dur":2.5}],"choice":null},"x_ns_auction":{"id":"x_ns_auction","act":3,"loc":"Nar Shaddaa: the Coin Room plaza, under the counting tower","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Coin Room. Where the Exchange sells what the Republic swears does not exist.","dur":4.6},{"who":"GOTO","line":"Lot forty-one. A Sith amulet, Tapani-era setting. Dark-side resonance confirmed by two appraisers, both since deceased.","dur":6.4},{"who":"GOTO","line":"Opening bid is eight thousand. The Exchange reminds bidders that it is the only bank on this moon that does not forget.","dur":6.4},{"who":"VESS","line":"That's the voice. Nobody's seen the droid since Malachor. The hologram still collects.","dur":4.8},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"A machine that outlived its masters.","dur":3.0},{"who":"GOTO","line":"I detect a new bidder. Unregistered. Interesting.","dur":3.6},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"Pay, and they believe you are a buyer. Take, and they learn what you are. Both are lessons. Choose which one they keep.","dur":6.6}],"choice":{"prompt":"The amulet waits under a ray-shield.","A":{"text":"Pay the Exchange. Let them think you are only a buyer.","consequence":"Smaller ambush, HEAT -3.","next":null,"set":null},"B":{"text":"Take it. Let them learn what you are.","consequence":"Hunters join the ambush, HEAT +10.","next":null,"set":null}}},"3_2b_the_lieutenant":{"id":"3_2b_the_lieutenant","act":3,"loc":"The Harbinger's hold: the Umbral Wake hangs in the tractor beam","shots":[{"who":"CAPTION","line":"The Umbral Wake hangs in the Harbinger's tractor beam, bleeding air.","dur":4.2},{"who":"DONN","line":"Please. I can fly. I can fly anything. I can be useful.","dur":4.0},{"who":"TRAYA","line":"A frightened man will tell you everything. A dead one tells the galaxy instead.","dur":5.2},{"who":"RATHATRI","line":"Nightbringer. Burn the old name off the hull.","dur":3.6}],"choice":{"prompt":"The lieutenant is still breathing in the wreck. Decide.","A":{"text":"Drag the lieutenant out alive.","consequence":"Interrogation intel on Jedi patrols. HEAT -2.","next":null,"set":null},"B":{"text":"Leave him in the drifting hulk.","consequence":"The rumor spreads: fear +10. HEAT +4.","next":null,"set":null}}}}};
